Review REVISION 15 of the ADDENDUM to the accepted RFC-257 WS-C (persistent pending writes and indexing sessions): DESIGN and IMPLEMENTATION together, as a DELTA gate. Repo /home/birdy/projects/fdb-go, branch upgrade/java-4.14.2.0, published as PR #786 (the owner's one PR for the whole upgrade). Candidate COMMIT 1c6059b91. The commits since revision 14 (1bc97d6af): f53cd6fc6 (CLAUDE.md and the umbrella RFC: the push rule), 5d95cd27c (WS-J step 2, gated with WS-J), and 1c6059b91, WS-C revision 15 (which also commits the WS-J design v16 gate's verdict files; those are not under review here). So revision 15 is `git diff 5d95cd27c 1c6059b91`. The addendum is section 7 of rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-c-design.md (design SHA256 34ebbcb27e016c0abfab1fff7e18294b3170c70ba91c8201049e222fc2b181c2, 2643 lines at 1c6059b91); 7.15 is revision 15, stating what changed and why, with evidence and the 7.14 sentences it supersedes. Revision 14's gate (rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-c-addendum-review-v14/): Torvalds NAK (six Lows), Graefe NAK (three Lows, nits), storage NAK (one Medium, four Lows, nits; over revisions 13 and 14). Read ws-c-addendum-review-v14/{graefe,torvalds,storage}.txt and check that EVERY finding and nit is resolved or answered, and that nothing revision 15 changed broke what revisions 12 to 14 fixed. The owner's rulings are in rfcs/257-java-4.14.2.0-upgrade.md, "Verification and review gates" item 9 (pre-release Go data unsupported; evidence red→green and Java-versus-Go, mutation runs only 0-3 per milestone where a test compares values that could move together or a pin cannot otherwise be shown to fire; one PR, pushed as it lands, CI and ACKs per workstream).
