Java sources: fdb-record-layer/fdb-record-layer-core/src/main/java/com/apple/foundationdb/record/: provider/foundationdb/{FDBRecordStore,OnlineIndexer,IndexingMultiTargetByRecords}.java, provider/foundationdb/indexes/{VectorIndexMaintainerFactory,VectorIndexHelper,VectorOptionKey,VectorIndexOptionKeys,HnswVectorIndexEngine,SlidingWindowIndexMaintainerFactory}.java, provider/common/DynamicMessageRecordSerializer.java, RecordMetaDataBuilder.java (union fields); fdb-record-layer/fdb-extensions/src/main/java/com/apple/foundationdb/linear/Metric.java; protobuf-java DynamicMessage/MapEntry behaviour (the re-save bytes are MEASURED by the JVM spec; say where you rely on source instead); JDK FloatingDecimal.readJavaFormatString and Enum.valueOf.
Tree objects: run `git show COMMIT:path` or `git diff A B -- path` from the repo root (the read-only policy admits commands that START with the git subcommand, or `git -C /home/birdy/projects/fdb-go ...`; avoid shell variables and `cd ... &&` chains). The working tree may move on; read commit objects. Logs under /var/tmp/fdb-upgrade-recovery/ may be read with the Read tool.
Actual reviewer gate run via `claude -p` (model opus, effort xhigh) under a read-only tool policy (Read/Grep/Glob plus read-only git/grep/sed Bash; no Edit/Write). No tests/probes/mutations/edits/staging/commits/push/CI/PR/publication/operational changes. Return ACK or NAK, the exact commit and design hash, and actionable findings with source line references ordered by severity. Incomplete review is not ACK. Under 900 words unless needed.
Preserved boundaries: approved Go raw/nullable-array/scalar/sorting extensions; LIMIT for queries; the materialized outer-join NLJ (RFC-152); C++ 7.3.77; format max 15 / default 14; no second query pipeline.
Distinguish measured facts from source hypotheses.

Apply the storage/wire lens: the record bytes Go writes for a type holding a map (new; replacing a record either engine wrote, under the preferred or an older union field; a map changed, built, with a key written twice, nested in a message, a map value or a repeated element), the index entries maintained on those saves and rebuilt by either engine over them, the VECTOR maintainer's configuration read from options either engine wrote, the CHANGELOG/DIVERGENCES statements a user relies on, and the owner's pre-release-data ruling.
